quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  31,12,"Surely, We blessed Luqman with wisdom, saying: ‘Be thankful to Allah. And whoever gives thanks gives thanks only for his (own) good. And whoever is thankless—then indeed Allah is All-Sufficient, All-Praised.’"
  31,13,"And when Luqman told his son, as he was counselling him: ‘O my son! Never associate any partners with Allah. Ascribing partners (to Allah) is indeed the worst injustice.’"
  31,14,"We have commanded human being regarding his parents (to honour them). His mother carried him with strain upon strain, and his weaning took two years: ‘So be grateful to Me and your parents. To Me will be the final return."
  31,15,"But if they urge you to associate (partners) with Me that you do not know about, then do not obey them. Yet keep their company in this world in a kind manner. But follow the way of those who turn to Me in true devotion. Then to Me will be your return, and I shall inform you what you used to do.’"
  31,16,"(Luqman continued:) ‘My son! Even if a deed were the weight of a mustard seed (hidden) in a rock, or (high above) in the heavens or (deep) in the earth, Allah will produce it (on the Day of Judgement). Indeed, Allah is All-Attentive, All-Aware."
  31,17,"My son! Establish the prayer, encourage what is good, forbid what is wrong and be patient through whatever befalls you. That is indeed a course worthy of high resolve."
  31,18,"Do not turn your face arrogantly away from people, nor walk exultantly on the land. Indeed, Allah does not like whoever is arrogant (or) boastful."
  31,19,"Be moderate in your pace. Lower your voice. Indeed, the most hateful of all voices is the braying of donkeys.’"
